  "sourceBoundContracts": [
    "Connected flat-row widths belong to independently cloned complete SwTableBox native frame-size items, with declaration widths limited to builder/import ingress. Shared legacy width requests author original boxes without forbidding native zero items; positive UI width admission remains separate.",
    "Native GetTabCols uses current-row visible and other-row hidden fuzzy boundaries/constraints; NewSetTabCols maps integer widths and adjusts actual original lines, honoring current-line unspanned apply. Writer forwards true current-line ruler flags to original document transaction and history.",
    "Original SaveTable attribute history and column-insertion retained sections include complete independent frame widths. Existing graph, nodes, cursor and repeated undo/redo owners stay native.",
    "Writer XML uses native row-box cumulative union boundaries with first-row total; source sorted-vector fuzzy20 lower bound insertion/find coalesces close boundaries. Actual cells carry spans and covered XML slots without duplicate native sections; browser borrows the same grid.",
    "ODF exports/imports represented flat independent cells, including source fuzzy20 normalization within tolerance. Browser codec copies all eight native frame-size fields and legacy ingress. No TextRuns translation is introduced."
  ],
  "residuals": [
    "Full merged/row-span/nested table graph propagation and selection, complete native XML styles and border formats remain incomplete.",
    "Box/line table native item pooling/UNO/format identity and full inherited attributes remain partial.",
    "Complete SFX bindings, VCL painting/ticks/snapping/protection/page/frame/paragraph/ruler state, RTL/vertical document dragging and collapsed-border pixel geometry remain partial.",
    "Native uint16 wrapped-delta equality, full VCL pixel-vector ownership/window/null offsets, column-margin modifier state and other full native contexts are not certified.",
    "Registered IO/open/save/recovery/settings remain byte-identical; no full module/upstream parity promotion."
  ]
}
